# Binary fixtures must never be line-ending converted.
#
# `git add` warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF" for a PNG and a PDF, which is a warning about
# a conversion that would corrupt them. It happened not to this time — the blobs are
# byte-identical to the working tree, verified with `cmp` — but the next fixture might not be so
# lucky, and a corrupted OCR fixture fails as "recognition found nothing", which reads like a
# defect in the recogniser rather than in the checkout.
#
# The `binary` macro is `-text -diff`: no conversion either way, and no attempt to diff them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary

# The AC-07 conformance vectors are deliberately pure ASCII with escaped inputs, so that an
# editor normalising Unicode on save cannot silently turn one case into another (§7.2). Line
# endings are part of that: a CRLF in a file whose whole purpose is byte-exact digests would
# move every vector below the change.
*.tsv -text
